@Atc.Kusto.Api.Sample_HostAddress = https://localhost:46612
@customerId=143

### GetCustomers

GET {{Atc.Kusto.Api.Sample_HostAddress}}/customers
Accept: application/json

### GetCustomerById

GET {{Atc.Kusto.Api.Sample_HostAddress}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Accept: application/json


### GetCustomerSales

GET {{Atc.Kusto.Api.Sample_HostAddress}}/customers/sales
Accept: application/json

### GetCustomersStream
GET {{Atc.Kusto.Api.Sample_HostAddress}}/customers/stream
Accept: application/json

### IngestDeviceReadings (default mode: ManagedStreaming -> 200 when streamed, 202 when it fell back to queued)
# Needs Ingestion:HostAddress / Ingestion:DatabaseName in appsettings and setup.kql from Atc.Kusto.Ingestion.Sample.
POST {{Atc.Kusto.Api.Sample_HostAddress}}/device-readings
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "deviceId": "device-1", "serialNumber": "SN-0001", "value": 21.5, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T08:00:00Z" },
  { "deviceId": "device-2", "serialNumber": "SN-0002", "value": 22.0, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T08:00:00Z" }
]

### IngestDeviceReadings queued (-> 202 Accepted)
POST {{Atc.Kusto.Api.Sample_HostAddress}}/device-readings?mode=Queued
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "deviceId": "device-3", "serialNumber": "SN-0003", "value": 19.0, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T08:05:00Z" }
]

### IngestDeviceReadings empty batch (-> 200 with status Skipped, cluster not contacted)
POST {{Atc.Kusto.Api.Sample_HostAddress}}/device-readings
Content-Type: application/json

[]

###
